msgid "Filter types"
msgstr "Tipos de filtro"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:51
msgid "Four pass‑zero configurations are supported:"
msgstr "Quatro configurações de passa‑zero são suportadas:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:77
msgid "Windows"
msgstr "Janelas"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:79
msgid ""
"The FIR design uses one of seven window functions to shape the filter's "
"frequency response:"
msgstr ""
"O projeto FIR usa uma de sete funções de janela para moldar a resposta "
"em frequência do filtro:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:112
msgid ""
"**Kaiser window** deserves special attention.  The shape parameter "
":math:`\\beta` controls the trade‑off between main‑lobe width and "
"sidelobe level.  The project includes a dedicated :math:`\\beta`-sweep "
"(``chaotic-pfc run sweep beta-sweep``) that evaluates Lyapunov exponents "
"across :math:`\\beta \\in [2, 14]` in steps of :math:`0.5` for each filter "
"type."
msgstr "**Kaiser window** deserves special attention.  The shape parameter :math:`\\beta` controls the trade‑off between main‑lobe width and sidelobe level.  The project includes a dedicated :math:`\\beta`-sweep (``chaotic-pfc run sweep beta-sweep``) that evaluates Lyapunov exponents across :math:`\\beta \\in [2, 14]` in steps of :math:`0.5` for each filter type."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:122
msgid "Stability and the fixed point"
msgstr "Estabilidade e o ponto fixo"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:124
msgid ""
"When an FIR filter is inserted into the Hénon feedback loop, the "
"Jacobian matrix grows from :math:`2 \\times 2` to :math:`(2 + N_c) "
"\\times (2 + N_c)`, where :math:`N_c` is the number of filter "
"coefficients that feed back into the dynamics."
msgstr ""
"Quando um filtro FIR é inserido no laço de realimentação do Hénon, a "
"matriz Jacobiana cresce de :math:`2 \\times 2` para :math:`(2 + N_c) "
"\\times (2 + N_c)`, onde :math:`N_c` é o número de coeficientes do filtro "
"que realimentam a dinâmica."

